<article class="env-lemma" id="0098">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0098">Lemma <span data-tag="0098">6.26.4</span>.</a> Let $(f, f^\sharp ) : (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y)$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-modules. Let $x \in X$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (f^*\mathcal{G})_ x = \mathcal{G}_{f(x)} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)}} \mathcal{O}_{X, x}  \]
</div>
  <p> as $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$-modules where the tensor product on the right uses $f^\sharp _ x : \mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)} \to \mathcal{O}_{X, x}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/008B" data-tag="008B">6.20.3</a> and the identification of the stalks of pullback sheaves at $x$ with the corresponding stalks at $f(x)$. See the formulae in Section <a href="/tag/008P" data-tag="008P">6.23</a> for example. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>